# Mobile navigation

The phone menu is isolated on purpose. Later page work must not fold it back into other components or paint over it.

## Where it lives

- Button, overlay, open animation, and scroll lock: `components/mobile-nav.tsx` only.
- It mounts on `document.body` (`#mobile-nav-root`), outside the header and outside page sections.
- Do not edit that file unless the user asked to change the phone menu.
- New links go in `lib/site-nav.ts`. Do not rebuild the menu to add a link.

## Layers

Use `siteLayerClass` from `lib/site-layers.ts`. Do not invent a new fixed z-index.

- Header `z-40`. Back to top `z-[80]`. Menu panel `z-[90]`. Menu button `z-[100]`. Fullscreen viewers `z-[120]`.
- Video and photo viewers portal to `document.body`, use the viewer layer, and stay above the menu.
- While a `role="dialog"` is open, `[data-scroll-top]` stays hidden (`app/globals.css`).

## Do not

- Put the menu button or overlay back inside the header, or inside anything with blur, transform, or animation.
- Change the fade-open, or add a circle wipe or full-screen blur on the menu.
- Raise another control above the menu button except a fullscreen viewer.
